{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse","id":1417647,"title":"Reaction of the Unconquered Sun to the Great Curse?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-11T08:51:38-07:00","id":1417647,"title":"Reaction of the Unconquered Sun to the Great Curse?","content":"Ok, I\u2019ve never played in 3rd Ed, so I am behind on all of the updated canon, but what should the response be from the UCS if he were to suddenly learn of the GC? He turned his back on Creation and nearly let the Great Contagion and the Fair Folk destroy it, all as a response to his Chosen\u2019s behavior. So what happens if he learns that a lot of them were ultimately innocent of their crimes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T11:19:23-07:00","id":1417665,"title":"","content":"The updated canon has said very little about the Unconquered Sun, in an intentional bid to focus more on human stories. We know he turned his face away from the Solars, we know that he speaks to some new Solars, and we know that he chooses new Solars (though it\u2019s unclear how conscious this is). I believe that any answers we gave would be headcanons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T11:39:45-07:00","id":1417671,"title":"","content":"Wait, he actively chooses Solars now? Didn\u2019t 2E have some VERY good reasons why Autocthon made that impossible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T11:53:48-07:00","id":1417673,"title":"","content":"It did. That change also made Exaltation feel more technical than awe-inspiring, and it made the UCS feel totally irrelevant to Solars\u2019 lived experience. Maybe there\u2019s still a tactical fallback option if the Solar-picker is killed, or maybe not! It hasn\u2019t been discussed In 3E canon and, I would guess, never will be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T12:10:08-07:00","id":1417677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1417671#post1417671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, he actively chooses Solars now? Didn\u2019t 2E have some VERY good reasons why Autocthon made that impossible?</div> </div> </div> </div>The main reason was Unnatural Mental Influence and Primordials being able to mind-control gods &quot;just because&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's not a thing in 3E.<br /> <br /> And if you kill someone because you are crazy, you still killed someone. Dad might be sad that he never saw your mental health problem and got you the help you need, but it doesn't bring your victim back to life.<br /> <br /> Cursed or not, the Exalted aren't innocent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T12:37:14-07:00","id":1417682,"title":"","content":"To me, it made Exaltation feel like it was something so grand that even the UCS had no real power over it. But I see where you are coming from. 2E was supposed to be incredibly arrogant and grandiose, and I understand that 3E is supposed to be about human sized adventures. Maybe level 20 Fighter humans, but still ultimately humans, like Tarzan and Hercules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T12:39:29-07:00","id":1417683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1417677#post1417677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main reason was Unnatural Mental Influence and Primordials being able to mind-control gods &amp;quot;just because&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> That's not a thing in 3E.<br /> <br /> And if you kill someone because you are crazy, you still killed someone. Dad might be sad that he never saw your mental health problem and got you the help you need, but it doesn't bring your victim back to life.<br /> <br /> Cursed or not, the Exalted aren't innocent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how you define ignorant. If your enemies were secretly pumping your water full of drugs that were guaranteed to warp your mind in dangerous ways, should you really be considered responsible for the consequences?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T13:59:25-07:00","id":1417698,"title":"","content":"So here's a take: maybe when someone tells him about the Great Curse, they realize from his response that on some level, conscious or unconscious, he already knew. He may or may not have known <i>exactly</i> why his Exalted were so unstable, but he's had a long time to think about the ways it might have been his fault. What stronger reason might there be to retreat from the world, to hide his face not just in disappointment but in shame?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T14:10:04-07:00","id":1417700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1417671#post1417671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, he actively chooses Solars now? Didn\u2019t 2E have some VERY good reasons why Autocthon made that impossible?</div> </div> </div> </div>The geas was supposed to be that the gods couldn't kill the Primordials, not that they couldn't disobey their commands. Making the Exaltations autonomous to respond to a change <i>that didn't need to be made</i> is not what I'd call a &quot;good reason.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T14:34:11-07:00","id":1417708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1417700#post1417700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The geas was supposed to be that the gods couldn't kill the Primordials, not that they couldn't disobey their commands. Making the Exaltations autonomous to respond to a change <i>that didn't need to be made</i> is not what I'd call a &quot;good reason.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What if the gods were geased not simply to do the Primordials no direct harm, but also had failsafes built into them so they could be ordered to stop if they were doing something indirectly harmful? Creation wasn\u2019t tailor made to the specifications of any one titan, so they probably left it so the \u201cindirect harm\u201d part of the geas required a specific command from the Titans since that would let them first debate with each other about what constituted \u201cindirect harm\u201d or \u201coffensiveness\u201d on a level that was unacceptable to any one titan\u2019s sensibilities. Remember, the Ebon Dragon hates everything on principal, and will try to collapse any system he can get his hands on because that is his nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 10-11-2020, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T15:02:27-07:00","id":1417712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1417708#post1417708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What if the gods were geased not simply to do the Primordials no direct harm, but also had failsafes built into them so they could be ordered to stop if they were doing something indirectly harmful? Creation wasn\u2019t tailor made to the specifications of any one titan, so they probably left it requiring a specific command from the Titans since that would let them first debate with each other about what constituted \u201cindirect harm\u201d or \u201coffensiveness\u201d on a level that was unacceptable. Remember, the Ebon Dragon hates everything on principal, and will try to collapse any system he can get his hands on because that is his nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's 2E Ebon Dragon. Little is known about him in Ex3 except what was written in 1E: that he forever tests the limits of his cage, and that he loves the doomed and dying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T15:37:30-07:00","id":1417719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1417712#post1417712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's 2E Ebon Dragon. Little is known about him in Ex3 except what was written in 1E: that he forever tests the limits of his cage, and that he loves the doomed and dying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite all of its many bugs, 2E will always be THE definitive Exalted to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T20:59:54-07:00","id":1417766,"title":"","content":"He may decide to share that information with Luna, the Maidens, and the sleeping Elemental Dragons.<br /> <br /> Then, he may decide to do nothing, as Creation is the domain of the Exalted, and all the Solars are currently there. Buuut... he may command Lytek, as the King of Heaven, to take action when a Solar wanders into Heaven. The first therapeutics would be, of course, experimental. But nobody's as full of hubris and has the kind of time as the Unconquered Sun, so I imagine after many (possibly fatal) trials, they get it right.<br /> <br /> How this process (and the deaths thereby) impact the reborn Solars' view of Heaven while they attempt to reassert some kind of influence in Creation is for the Solar players to decide... if they're playing a 2e-inspired, 'rattle the cage of the gods'-themed campaign. It may never come up in your 3e campaign, with all that time spent with swords and sandals!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T09:57:56-07:00","id":1417846,"title":"","content":"The misunderstanding that UCS can't choose solars even while his main body is preoccupied with other things is a fundamental misunderstanding of the fact that Exaltation is a capital-M Miracle, with all the religious connotations thereof, in-setting. The Incarnae are existences above and apart from ordinary gods and thus their awareness need not be limited to a singular perspective. The Exaltations will continue to circulate even after their deaths, and those empowered by them will still be considered Chosen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T12:05:09-07:00","id":1417862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1417712#post1417712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's 2E Ebon Dragon. Little is known about him in Ex3 except what was written in 1E: that he forever tests the limits of his cage, and that he loves the doomed and dying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really important question and here is as good a place to ask it as any<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve never actually read the 2E core book. Is it true that a lot of the 2E lore has been retconned by 3E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T12:53:31-07:00","id":1417881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1417862#post1417862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really important question and here is as good a place to ask it as any<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve never actually read the 2E core book. Is it true that a lot of the 2E lore has been retconned by 3E?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem wasn't really the 2E core, it was the lore that built up over 2E's lifespan (e.g. denigrating the Dragon-Blooded, magitech as the apex of artifacts, the increasing focus on high-level stuff like the Primordials and Incarnae towards its end, moving away from Creation itself). And much of <i>that</i>, specifically, has gone by the wayside in 3E.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T15:42:56-07:00","id":1417936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1417862#post1417862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really important question and here is as good a place to ask it as any<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve never actually read the 2E core book. Is it true that a lot of the 2E lore has been retconned by 3E?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but a lot of that is stuff that 2E retconned from 1E.<br /> <br /> 2E and 3E are both reimaginings of the original lore. 2E is a lot closer in content to 1E, as huge sections were simply copy-pasted. But 3E is much closer in <u><i>tone and intent</i></u> to 1E.<br /> <br /> Heck, even 1E retconned 1E so it's not like there's a &quot;pure&quot; Exalted out there.<br /> <br /> I like 2E, a lot. But, on the whole, the 3E lore is better -- it makes it easier to tell interesting stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T15:43:31-07:00","id":1417937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1417881#post1417881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem wasn't really the 2E core, it was the lore that built up over 2E's lifespan (e.g. denigrating the Dragon-Blooded, magitech as the apex of artifacts, the increasing focus on high-level stuff like the Primordials and Incarnae towards its end, moving away from Creation itself). And much of <i>that</i>, specifically, has gone by the wayside in 3E.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a really good idea. I like 3e so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T16:56:43-07:00","id":1417950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1417881#post1417881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> denigrating the Dragon-Blooded</div> </div> </div> </div>What did they do specifically that denigrated the Dragon Blooded? I thought they were always an imperialist empire on the brink of collapse due to the weight of its flaws and the lack of its central authority figure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T19:10:32-07:00","id":1417974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1417950#post1417950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did they do specifically that denigrated the Dragon Blooded? I thought they were always an imperialist empire on the brink of collapse due to the weight of its flaws and the lack of its central authority figure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the Realm in specific. Over the course of 2e the role of Dragon-Blooded seemed to slip more and more, the Usurpation becoming more cosmically wrong (the Exalted Mandate to Rule Creation now specifically defined as specifically applying to the Celestial Exalted), to the point that one book called out that a god would show a humble street urchin more respect intuitively than they would a Terrestrial, as the urchin had the capacity to Exalt as a Celestial, which the Terrestrial never would.<br /> <br /> There is a tremendous difference for calling out a failing, flawed empire, and going &quot;Oh my GOD, you Exalted as a Dragon-Blooded? Oh I'm so sorry. Don't worry, though, I could always use another lackey. I even have another one of you, and I think you'd make great babies for the next generation.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":". 10-12-2020, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T21:38:52-07:00","id":1417989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1417936#post1417936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but a lot of that is stuff that 2E retconned from 1E.<br /> <br /> 2E and 3E are both reimaginings of the original lore. 2E is a lot closer in content to 1E, as huge sections were simply copy-pasted. But 3E is much closer in <u><i>tone and intent</i></u> to 1E.<br /> <br /> Heck, even 1E retconned 1E so it's not like there's a &quot;pure&quot; Exalted out there.<br /> <br /> I like 2E, a lot. But, on the whole, the 3E lore is better -- it makes it easier to tell interesting stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without getting too far off-track for this thread, 1E had a lot of great ideas that posed some tonal challenges. When I was tasked with translating the Immaculate Order from 1E to 3E, I changed little of its substance, but got some feedback that it felt like more of a living religion. 2E had gone in the opposite direction, emphasizing the Immaculate Order's lies, which--in the minds of many fans--made its followers rubes.<br /> <br /> Edit: I feel I should clarify: the major changes from prior editions were things I was told to write. I just wrote them with an eye toward relatability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 10-19-2020, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T22:42:58-07:00","id":1417990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1417950#post1417950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did they do specifically that denigrated the Dragon Blooded? I thought they were always an imperialist empire on the brink of collapse due to the weight of its flaws and the lack of its central authority figure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 2E did this thing over and over where it emphasized that DBs weren't really Exalted compared to Celestials. Like how the gods of Yu Shan are described as seeing DBs as even below mortals, because at least a mortal MIGHT Celestial Exalt. The mechanics didn't do much to help the issue as 2e DB Charms... well look at their defenses. How many of them even work against a foe strong enough that you'd need the Charm in the first place? And oh god... the breeding camps.<br /> <br /> 3E has bent over itself to move away from that and emphasize that DBs, while the weakest of the Exalted in broad stroke sense, are still Exalted demigods who blood courses with the raw elements of Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T04:14:09-07:00","id":1418015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1417989#post1417989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without getting too far off-track for this thread, 1E had a lot of great ideas that posed some tonal challenges. When I was tasked with translating the Immaculate Order from 1E to 3E, I changed little of its substance, but got some feedback that it felt like more of a living religion. 2E had gone in the opposite direction, emphasizing the Immaculate Order's lies, which--in the minds of many fans--made its followers rubes.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the Immaculate Order is a more legit religion in 3e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T10:12:34-07:00","id":1418064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1418015#post1418015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the Immaculate Order is a more legit religion in 3e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The Order is certainly wielded toward certain agendas and political order, like any real world politically powerful religious institutions.- but the philosophy itself actually developed on its own among Dragon-Blooded in the Shogunate period before the Bronze faction co-opted it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T13:12:21-07:00","id":1418082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1418064#post1418064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. The Order is certainly wielded toward certain agendas and political order, like any real world politically powerful religious institutions.- but the philosophy itself actually developed on its own among Dragon-Blooded in the Shogunate period before the Bronze faction co-opted it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T08:44:29-07:00","id":1418197,"title":"","content":"Re: UCS directly choosing Solars, there\u2019s an implication at least by omission that it might (usually) be an unconscious process going on in the back of his head somewhere that he couldn\u2019t stop even if he wanted to, rather than something he actually <i>controls</i> in the usual sense of the word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T20:19:17-07:00","id":1418930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1418064#post1418064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. The Order is certainly wielded toward certain agendas and political order, like any real world politically powerful religious institutions.- but the philosophy itself actually developed on its own among Dragon-Blooded in the Shogunate period before the Bronze faction co-opted it.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does that work with the fiction of the Immaculate Dragons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T23:31:56-07:00","id":1418946,"title":"","content":"The Immaculate Dragons are composites of historical Dragon-Blooded. There may or may not have really been a Mela but some portion of the acts attributed to her by the Immaculate Texts are things that really happened. Which, if you replace \u201csome portion\u201d with \u201call (or at least all the important ones),\u201d is actually something the Order considers it acceptable to know if you\u2019re deemed wise and pious enough to not suddenly lose your faith over it.<br /> <br /> Similarly, in 3e \u201cPossessing demons wielding stolen power\u201d is considered the lies-for-children version of the nature of Solars and Lunars, and an experienced monk could point you to the part of the Texts in which the official story is actually \u201cThe Sun and Moon Exalting people was a mistake, turns out their Essence is less than fully compatible with the human souls and <i>will</i> turn you into someone comparable to the tyrants of the Age of Nightmares.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 10-19-2020, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T12:31:46-07:00","id":1419623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1417990#post1417990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3E has bent over itself to move away from that and emphasize that DBs, while the weakest of the Exalted in broad stroke sense, are still Exalted demigods who blood courses with the raw elements of Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I really like about 3e (even if I have problems with quite a lot of other things) was how much DBs can stand up to other Exalts through Evocations. The Wild Hunt having all of those artifacts on hand is an actual difference maker when it comes to hunting down the local Lunar, and I wish that some of the stuff that was cut for DBs in regards to artifacts was kept instead in order to better maintain that advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T12:58:54-07:00","id":1419628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1419623#post1419623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I really like about 3e (even if I have problems with quite a lot of other things) was how much DBs can stand up to other Exalts through Evocations. The Wild Hunt having all of those artifacts on hand is an actual difference maker when it comes to hunting down the local Lunar, and I wish that some of the stuff that was cut for DBs in regards to artifacts was kept instead in order to better maintain that advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What was cut?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T14:34:58-07:00","id":1419645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1419628#post1419628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What was cut?</div> </div> </div> </div>There were three tiers of evocations, like with sorcery. Emerald, Sapphire and Adamant- they're still mentioned in Design Beyond Limit in the corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T15:56:44-07:00","id":1419668,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s still around, after a fashion - it\u2019s just that we\u2019ve got Dissonant, neutral, and Resonant Evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T17:51:36-07:00","id":1419687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1419645#post1419645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There were three tiers of evocations, like with sorcery. Emerald, Sapphire and Adamant- they're still mentioned in Design Beyond Limit in the corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What does that have to do with Dragon-Blooded maintaining their strength via evocations? They still get the Resonant effects with Jade in the RAW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T19:45:46-07:00","id":1419696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1419628#post1419628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What was cut?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was going to be a mechanic whereby DBs auto-pick up or generate Evocations that their &quot;ancestors&quot; used, which would help them stand up to Solars (Being Resonant in All Materials vs. Being resonant in <i>most</i> Materials (as Jade is five different types) and auto-obtaining Evocations the moment you attune to an Artifact.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T23:44:43-07:00","id":1419725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1419696#post1419696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was going to be a mechanic whereby DBs auto-pick up or generate Evocations that their &quot;ancestors&quot; used, which would help them stand up to Solars (Being Resonant in All Materials vs. Being resonant in <i>most</i> Materials (as Jade is five different types) and auto-obtaining Evocations the moment you attune to an Artifact.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s literally what heirloom artifacts are. DBs of a given House or Gen get an automatic free evocation when attuned to one of their ancestral artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T11:48:22-07:00","id":1419824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1419725#post1419725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s literally what heirloom artifacts are. DBs of a given House or Gen get an automatic free evocation when attuned to one of their ancestral artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welp, I'm officially an idiot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T14:47:11-07:00","id":1419848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1418946#post1418946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Immaculate Dragons are composites of historical Dragon-Blooded. There may or may not have really been a Mela but some portion of the acts attributed to her by the Immaculate Texts are things that really happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless 3e changed this, I thought that the Immaculate Dragons <i>were</i> real, they're just souls of Gaia sleeping at the poles. It's the Immaculate Philosophy's conception of them as humanoid beings that helped kill the Solars that's the lie.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T17:20:08-07:00","id":1419867,"title":"","content":"The key in 3e is that &quot;Chosen of the Unconquered Sun&quot; is a literally true statement; the Unconquered Sun <i>chose</i> you. The exact psychology or mechanism of the choosing is unspecified, and what would happen if the Unconquered Sun were killed is unspecified, but if you're a Solar, you were chosen by the Unconquered Sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T17:27:01-07:00","id":1419869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1419848#post1419848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless 3e changed this, I thought that the Immaculate Dragons <i>were</i> real, they're just souls of Gaia sleeping at the poles. It's the Immaculate Philosophy's conception of them as humanoid beings that helped kill the Solars that's the lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are the Five Elemental Dragons, and then there are the Immaculate Dragons, &quot;the Five Elemental Dragons . . . incarnated in five specific individuals&quot; (as the core book puts it).<br /> <br /> The former certainly exist. As to the latter, per page 90 of The Realm:<br /> <br /> Popular myth states that the Immaculate Order was born when the Elemental Dragons incarnated to lead the Dragon-Blooded in glorious rebellion against the demonic Anathema, raising the Dragon-Blooded to their rightful place as Princes of the Earth. This view of history suffices for most lay mortals, and even for incurious Dragon-Blooded, whose station doesn\u2019t demand the full truth. Once a monk has received sufficient spiritual preparation, she learns a more nuanced history: that the Immaculate Order was founded during the Dragon-Blooded Shogunate, that the Immaculate Dragons\u2019 great deeds are allegories condensed from dozens of historical Dragon-Blooded across various time periods, and that the Solar and Lunar Anathema are Exalted themselves, though doomed to insanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T05:10:56-07:00","id":1419967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417647-reaction-of-the-unconquered-sun-to-the-great-curse?p=1419848#post1419848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless 3e changed this, I thought that the Immaculate Dragons <i>were</i> real, they're just souls of Gaia sleeping at the poles. It's the Immaculate Philosophy's conception of them as humanoid beings that helped kill the Solars that's the lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Minor nitpick:<br /> <br /> In 1E and 3E the Five Elemental Dragons are Gaia's children, not her souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}